  "Accepted Answers": [],
  "Unordered Answers": false,
  "Solution": "A diagonal divides the square into 2 isosceles right triangles. By the Pythagorean theorem, the diagonal length is \\(\\sqrt{2^2+2^2}=2\\sqrt{2}\\).",
